{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Eviction for criminal conviction, theft, or human trafficking","requirement":"A landlord may evict a tenant convicted of or civilly liable for assault, threats, theft, drug activity, or human trafficking, or who knowingly harbors such a person. Suit must be filed within two years, after a three-day Notice to Quit.","key_value":"2-year filing limit; 3-day Notice to Quit","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenants; covers convictions, juvenile delinquency findings, and civil liability for offenses on the premises or against the landlord, family, or employees.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Subsection (p) does not apply where the tenant allows a juvenile found delinquent for drug use or possession to reside at the property.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1","quoted_span":"The landlord may file for eviction, if the tenant has been convicted of or pleaded guilty to, or if a juvenile has been found by the court to be delinquent due to an offense involving assault or terrorist threats against the landlord, a member of the landl ord’s family or an employee of the landlord.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Owner-occupied two- and three-family dwelling eviction causes and notice","requirement":"A landlord of an owner-occupied two- or three-family dwelling may remove a tenant only by court order and only for specified causes, serving a three-month, one-month, or three-day Notice to Quit as applicable.","key_value":"3-month / 1-month / 3-day notice to quit","coverage_conditions":"Landlord-occupied two- and three-family dwellings; tenants staying past the lease term, not paying rent, disorderly, willfully damaging, or violating rules or lease provisions.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":2,"max_units":3,"owner_dependent":true,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.2","quoted_span":"A three (3) month notice to quit must be gi ven if an at will tenancy or year -to-year tenancy exists. A one (1) month notice to quit is required for a month-to-month tenancy and other types of tenancies are entitled to a one (1) month notice to quit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Rooming and boarding house eviction good cause and notice","requirement":"Owners of rooming and boarding houses must follow the good causes and notice requirements of the Eviction Law when evicting residents, unless the Bureau orders otherwise, and must give the County Welfare Board at least three working days' notice before starting an eviction.","key_value":"3 working days' notice to County Welfare Board","coverage_conditions":"Rooming and boarding houses with at least two living units occupied by unrelated persons without private kitchens and bathrooms, subject to statutory exceptions.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":2,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Rooming and boarding houses"},"exemptions":"Hotels with more than 85 percent temporary occupancy, school and college dormitories, buildings housing only college students, and certain residences for the disabled.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.A.C. 5:27-3.3(c)","quoted_span":"The Regulations Governing Rooming and Boarding Houses, which are enforced by the Bureau of Rooming and Boarding House Standards of the Department of Community Affairs, require owners of rooming and boarding houses to follow the good causes and notice requirements of the Eviction Law when evicting residents, except if otherwise ordered by the Bureau (N.J.A.C. 5:27-3.3(c)).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Penalties for eviction on owner-occupancy or demolition grounds","requirement":"A landlord who evicts a tenant to personally occupy the unit must occupy it for at least six months; a landlord who evicts to demolish or permanently retire a building from residential use may not use the property residentially for five years.","key_value":"6 months' owner occupancy; 5-year residential use bar","coverage_conditions":"Landlords who gave notice of intent to personally occupy a unit, or to permanently board up, demolish, or retire the building from residential use.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Treble damages plus attorney fees and costs; for demolition-ground violations, treble damages plus a civil penalty up to $10,000 per violation and a five-year bar on planned real estate development registration.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.6","quoted_span":"When a tenant vacates a dwelling unit after having been given notice that the landlord wishes to personally occupy the unit the landlord must occupy the unit for at least six (6) months.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Anti-reprisal protection for tenants","requirement":"A landlord may not retaliate by eviction, substantial lease alteration, or refusal to renew when a tenant enforces lease or legal rights, makes a good faith complaint about health or safety violations, organizes, or refuses a retaliatory lease change.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All rental properties used for dwelling purposes, including mobile homes, except owner-occupied two- or three-family dwellings.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied two- and three-family dwellings"},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied two- and three-family dwellings.","penalty":"Tenant may sue the landlord for damages in a civil action.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:42-10.10","quoted_span":"A landlord cannot take reprisal action against a tenant by eviction, substantial alteration of a lease or its terms, or refusal to renew a lease when a tenant exercises certain civil rights (N.J.S.A. 2A:42-10.10).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Foreclosure eviction 90-day notice requirement","requirement":"Foreclosure alone is not grounds for eviction; before evicting a tenant because a buyer will personally occupy the foreclosed property, the owner must give a 90-day notice to quit, and a new owner must notify tenants within 10 business days after the sale.","key_value":"90-day notice to quit","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenants in foreclosed properties; month-to-month tenants and two- and three-family owner-occupied units are not exempt from the 90-day notice requirement.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Foreclosed residential rental properties"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:50-69","quoted_span":"Before a tenant can be evicted due to foreclosure, the landlord must provide the tenant with a 90 -day notice to qui t when the foreclosed property has been purchased by a buyer who wants to personally occupy it as his or her primary residence.","interaction":"Federal law does not preempt any State or local law that provides longer time periods or other additional protections for tenants in foreclosure proceedings.","confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Senior Citizens and Disabled Protected Tenancy on conversion","requirement":"Qualifying senior, disabled, or disabled-veteran tenants who lived in a building at least one year before a conversion to condominium, cooperative, or fee simple ownership may be protected from eviction for 40 years.","key_value":"40 years","coverage_conditions":"Tenants at least 62, permanently disabled, or disabled veterans (60% or higher) who lived in the building one year before the conversion recording; family income no more than three times the county per-person average or $50,000, whichever is greater.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Senior, disabled, and disabled-veteran tenants in buildings being converted"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.28","quoted_span":"Tenants may be protected from eviction for 40 years if their family income is not more than three (3) times the average per person income in their county or $50,000.00, whichever is greater (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.28).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Tenant Protection Act of 1992 conversion protections","requirement":"Extends protected-tenancy protections to qualified tenants in qualified counties (currently only Hudson County) in buildings converted or being converted who were not eligible under the 1981 Senior Citizens and Disabled Protected Tenancy Act.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Qualified tenants in qualified counties — currently only Hudson County — in buildings converted or being converted, not eligible under the 1981 Act.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Qualified counties; currently only Hudson County"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.40","quoted_span":"The Tenant Protection Law of 1992 amendment extends protections to qualified tenants in qualified counties in buildings converted or being converted who were not eligible for Protected Tenancy as either Senior Citizens or Disabled Persons under the “Senior Citizens and Disabled Protected Tenancy Act of 1981”","interaction":null,"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Prohibition on rent increases above rent control or unconscionable increases","requirement":"A landlord may not increase rent above the limit set by a rent control or rent leveling ordinance, or, where the property is not subject to rent control, impose an unreasonable or unconscionable rent increase.","key_value":"rent control or rent leveling ordinance limit","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental properties subject to a rent control or rent leveling ordinance, or not subject to rent control, as part of a list of prohibited landlord conduct.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":null,"quoted_span":"An increase in rent in excess of any rent control or rent leveling ordinance, or if the property is not subject to rent control, an unreasonable or unconscionable rent increase.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.4,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
